    <solution><alert>  SOLUTION </alert>



The function <m>f(x) = -3 - 8 \cos{( 80 \pi x)}</m> has midline <m>y = k = -3</m> and amplitude <m>| A | = 8</m>.  Since <m>B = 80 \pi</m>, the period is
<me>\mbox{period} = \frac{ 2 \pi}{B} = \frac{2 \pi}{80 \pi} = \frac{1}{40}.</me>
Since this is a cosine function with a negative value for the parameter <m>A = - 8</m>, when <m>x = 0</m> the graph is at its minimum value.  Therefore the correct answer is graph D .



</solution>
